WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.669
-First of all, "Mr. Robot" --
-Yeah.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.336
-Congrats.
That's such a great show.

00:00:04.336 --> 00:00:06.939
You know, I've had you -- we've
had you on talking about that.

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:09.976
Is it true, I heard, that it
might be coming to an end?

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.478
-It's so sad. Yes.

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:14.414
-Why?
-I don't know. I don't know.

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.582
[ Laughter ]
Because I love it so much.

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:18.784
I'm quite frankly
a bit disappointed.

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:22.856
But Sam Esmail, who writes,
creates and directs it

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:24.891
and is the genius mind behind it

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:28.327
had a finite period of time
he wanted to tell this story.

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:31.931
And it's coming to
its conclusion this year.

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:34.633
-Gosh.
-But, you know, the best part

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:37.370
of it is that I wouldn't have
had this role had the producers

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.739
not seen me on "Mr. Robot."

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.674
I wouldn't have got the role
of Freddie Mercury.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.442
-Is that right?
-So that's a pretty cool thing.

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:44.844
-Absolutely.
-Yes.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.645
-And you got an Emmy for it,
as well.

00:00:46.645 --> 00:00:47.880
-Yes.
-I think it's --

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.082
[ Laughter ]
You did, I mean, yeah.

00:00:50.082 --> 00:00:51.951
-I have to remind myself I did.
-You got an Emmy. Yeah.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:54.019
[ Cheers and applause ]
You're good.

00:00:54.019 --> 00:00:56.456
Remind yourself.
-Yes, thank you.

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:59.158
-Let's talk about --
-Let's chat.

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:02.962
-..."Bohemian rhapsody,"
because if I had your e-mail,

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:05.197
your phone number, I would have
called you a gazillion times

00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:06.432
and said, "Dude,
you were unbelievable!

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:07.633
You were unbelievable
in this movie!"

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:08.834
-You have my e-mail
and phone number.

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:11.905
-That's true.
But I decided to not call you.

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:12.872
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.842
I -- I flipped out.
-Did you?

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.178
-You were unbelievable.
-Thanks, man.

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:20.146
-I mean, 'cause, dude,
this is -- I mean, look,

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.013
this is you right here.

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:22.214
This is supermodel,

00:01:22.214 --> 00:01:24.417
actor Rami Malek right here,
by the way.

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.519
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.388
Congrats on this cover,
by the way.

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:29.989
-Isn't that nice?
-Is this true --

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:31.558
-I didn't think that
would ever happen.

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:34.961
-This the first ever "GQ"
in the Middle East.

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.262
-Yes.
-They never had this.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.097
-If ever I was going to be on
the "GQ,"

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:39.766
it would be the "GQ"
in the Middle East.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.967
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. That's kind of amazing

00:01:41.967 --> 00:01:43.202
for you, right?
-Yeah. It's huge.

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:45.338
I mean, my family is Egyptian.

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:47.574
I'm a first-generation American.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:50.843
So, you know, being Egyptian

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.611
is in the fiber of my DNA

00:01:52.611 --> 00:01:54.447
and something I'm immensely
proud of.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:57.717
So to grace this cover
is an accomplishment.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.819
I never would have thought
I would be saying that,

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:00.687
but it really is.

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:01.954
-It's a big deal.
-Yeah.

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:03.022
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:07.126
-This guy --
you don't look like --

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:09.762
You don't look like
Freddie Mercury, to me.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.264
I wouldn't --
I wouldn't cast you.

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:12.899
-I didn't think so either, yeah.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:14.200
-But then when you see
this movie --

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:18.104
Guys, look at this --
side by side.

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:20.139
That's Rami.

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:21.507
[ Applause ]

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:23.542
Dude, you are unbelievable.

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:26.145
I mean, I freaked out.
I mean, I'm watching scenes,

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:29.148
And I go,
"Is that a real clip of --

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:30.649
the real clip of Live Aid?"

00:02:30.649 --> 00:02:33.720
When you're going out,
it's just you going from behind.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.655
And I go -- I mean, even
your posture is different

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:37.156
than your own posture.
-Yeah, yeah, it is.

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:39.058
-Right, because this is
probably how in "Mr. Robot",

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.693
this is your posture.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:44.096
I mean, he's so -- I have these
teeth that I wear, exactly.

00:02:44.096 --> 00:02:45.265
I have these teeth that I wear.

00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:46.832
And the first time
I put them in my mouth,

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:49.835
I was incredibly insecure.

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:51.804
And then I found myself
compensating.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:54.406
I just started sitting up
straight and being more elegant.

00:02:54.406 --> 00:02:56.542
And he had the best posture.
And you start to think,

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:59.579
"Oh, these are the reasons
he is who he is."

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:01.481
-Wow, that's interesting.
-It is, right?

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:02.749
-And you just rock it, dude.

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:04.784
I can't even believe you --
I mean, how did you even

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:06.518
pull off the Live Aid thing?

00:03:06.518 --> 00:03:08.721
-You're not gonna believe this.

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:12.525
One of the greatest rock
performances in history.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:15.294
It's considered maybe
the greatest.

00:03:15.294 --> 00:03:18.998
For some reason, our producers
thought it would be a good idea

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.267
to start with that on day one.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.335
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:24.037
-That was the first day
of shooting?

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:25.738
-That was the first day, man.
-Wow!

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.606
-So, I --
-Wow!

00:03:27.606 --> 00:03:30.176
-About halfway into the day,
I thought, "Oh, man."

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:33.012
-Jump into the fire, man.
-I jumped -- trial by fire,

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.914
entire baptism by fire.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:38.785
But I thought, "They must have
reason for doing this."

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:40.920
Because, you know,
if halfway through they get --

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:44.356
we get through this and we suck,
they'll just pull the plug

00:03:44.356 --> 00:03:47.160
on the whole production,
pack it up and go home, right?"

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.995
-Smart, yeah, you save
a lot of money that way.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:49.862
-Save $60 million.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.163
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:53.766
We don't have to watch
this B-rate version of Queen

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:54.800
for three months.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.302
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:59.271
-When I got the call sheet
for day two,

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:00.873
it was like winning an Oscar.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.508
[ Laughter ]
-It's like -- really.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:05.044
-We're back!
-"We are making this movie.

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:06.312
This is great."
-It's happening!

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:08.347
-You wore the white tank
and the jeans.

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:11.751
-Yeah. It's surreal
walking out there

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:14.419
after watching that concert
so many times and --

00:04:14.419 --> 00:04:17.256
-Did you feel at any point --
you must as an actor,

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:19.258
but did you feel at one point
you're like,

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:21.694
"I actually am turning into
Freddie Mercury."

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:24.296
When did you feel?
Like when you put the teeth in,

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:26.199
or -- Who did your --
-The teeth helped.

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:27.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.968
-You'll see it.
I mean, you'll see.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.403
-They're there. I'm warning you.

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:31.537
-They're definitely there, yeah.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:32.371
-They're there. But, I mean,

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:34.173
he got called "Bucky" as a kid

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:36.308
before he was even called
Freddie Mercury.

00:04:36.308 --> 00:04:37.843
And I won't tell you
his real name.

00:04:37.843 --> 00:04:39.712
If you don't know, you'll have
to find out in the movie.

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:40.546
Don't Google it, please.

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:41.747
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:44.450
But you put the teeth in,
and that's one thing.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.985
I had this exceptional makeup
artist named Jan Sewell.

00:04:46.985 --> 00:04:49.955
She did Eddie Redmayne
in "The Theory of Everything."

00:04:49.955 --> 00:04:51.757
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Remember that transformation?

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:53.759
I'm like, "I get her? Amazing."
-Wow!

00:04:53.759 --> 00:04:56.295
And then I had Julian Day
do the costumes.

00:04:56.295 --> 00:04:59.332
And these costumes, maybe...
-The best.

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:00.899
-...100 different outfits,
right?

00:05:00.899 --> 00:05:02.035
-If you're a fan of Queen,

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:03.735
the costumes alone
will get applause.

00:05:03.735 --> 00:05:06.639
-Right? They will.
And they do.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:07.606
-They do?
-They do.

00:05:07.606 --> 00:05:08.708
-I would go nuts for you.
-Yeah.

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:10.410
-I was like, "That is classic!"
-Yeah.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.577
-Only Freddie Mercury
could pull that off.

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:13.012
-Only Freddie Mercury.
And it's a long way

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:15.414
from "Mr. Robot" where I wear
one thing every single day.

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:16.882
[ Laughter ]
-You wear a hoodie.

00:05:16.882 --> 00:05:17.884
-Yeah.
-You wear a hoodie, yeah.

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:19.118
-That's it.
-That's it, yeah.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.519
-I mean, talk about
polar opposites.

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:22.788
-But do you know how to play
the piano?

00:05:22.788 --> 00:05:24.423
-I've never played the piano.

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:25.858
I was scared
of playing the piano.

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:28.027
As a kid, it seemed like
such a foreign thing.

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:29.695
I told them when I sat down,
I go,

00:05:29.695 --> 00:05:32.631
"Listen, guys, I'm not going to
be the Hollywood actor

00:05:32.631 --> 00:05:34.000
that sells myself here.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.802
I don't play the piano.

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:37.236
I don't think I'm a singer.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:40.239
I have a very unusual way
of dancing.

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:41.540
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.543
That's about as close as I can
get to Freddie Mercury."

00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:45.311
-And they still hired you?
-I think they thought,

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:47.846
"Oh, here we'd get
a humble actor for once.

00:05:47.846 --> 00:05:49.982
[ Laughter ]
There's a modest guy."

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:51.851
Yeah.
-You just hit a home run.

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:53.352
They got to be -- everyone's
got to be so psyched

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:54.720
for your performance.
-Oh, man.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.121
-I mean, you at one point
played the piano

00:05:56.121 --> 00:05:57.356
laying upside down.

00:05:57.356 --> 00:05:58.558
You were laying on the ground
playing it

00:05:58.558 --> 00:06:00.893
with your hands crossed.
-Spoiler alert.

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:01.694
-Oh, sorry. Yeah, yeah.

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:02.862
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:04.196
-Please. Stop.
-Please, there's other ones.

00:06:04.196 --> 00:06:08.634
-No, no, no. That was something
Freddie did every night.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:11.570
And the man never ceases
to amaze me.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:14.373
As much prep as I did,

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:17.476
I found out more and more about
what he was capable of.

00:06:17.476 --> 00:06:21.447
And I tried to do him honor
and --

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:23.316
-You did.
-Yeah.

00:06:23.316 --> 00:06:26.085
He is a magnificent human being.

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:27.920
And I can't wait to share
this movie

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:29.421
with a brand-new generation.

00:06:29.421 --> 00:06:31.457
-Oh, just so cool.
I want to show a clip.

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:34.827
-Show it.
-This is Rami Malek

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:37.563
as Freddie Mercury
in "Bohemian Rhapsody."

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:38.931
Take a look at this.

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:42.869
-What's going on?
-You'd know if you were on time.

00:06:42.869 --> 00:06:46.038
-I want to give the audience
a song that they can perform.

00:06:46.038 --> 00:06:47.606
-So what can they do?

00:06:47.606 --> 00:06:50.476
[ Stomping and clapping
rhythmically ]

00:06:56.415 --> 00:07:01.053
-Imagine thousands of people
doing this in unison.

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:04.724
Huh?

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:06.926
-What's the lyric?

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:09.829
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:12.964 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:12.964 --> 00:07:18.838
-♪ We will, we will rock you ♪

00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:21.740
-♪ We will, we will ♪

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:24.577
-♪ Rock you ♪

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:27.113
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:28.548
-Rami Malek, everybody.

